checkup=3.3
pots=1.4
# clinical=1.8: Medication RDF type and predicates migrated from health: to clinical: namespace
#
# 2026-07-15 batched draft sync (spec PENDING_DOWNSTREAM_SYNC rows 1-3). Per
# D-PATH, pre-stable drafts stay UNROWED until v1.0 graduation; the namespaces +
# predicates were registered in vocabularies/namespaces.py without a version row:
#   - evidence@v1-draft.0.2: verdict-taxonomy-v2 facet predicates (direction,
#     basis, strength, settled, reason, confidence) + the evidence namespace.
#   - workbench@v1-draft.0.4: workbench:userSourceLabel + the workbench namespace.
#   - workbench@v1-draft.0.5 notes substrate: external namespaces oa, ical, skos
#     registered so oa:Annotation notes (incl. the workbench:followUp motivation
#     individual) round-trip. No JSON-LD context for drafts yet.
#
# core=3.4: pod export manifest. All 32 terms core v3.4 defines are registered.
#     ExportManifest / RecordSummary / InteractionScenario / DeviceSource
#     dataclasses added, with serialize_export_manifest(), parse_export_manifest()
#     and Pod.manifest(). ExportManifest is modelled on dcat:Dataset, so its
#     descriptive fields map to dcterms:, not to Cascade-specific inventions.
#     RecordSummary is modelled on void:Dataset: RECORD_SUMMARY_COUNT_CLASSES
#     pairs each entity count with the void:class it counts, and
#     RECORD_SUMMARY_DAY_COUNTS keeps the five day counts out of that set
#     because they count days covered, not entities. Reading-level cascade:date,
#     cascade:sampleCount and cascade:loincCode registered on the history-entry
#     types. The dcat / void namespaces are registered as URI constants only —
#     the SDK does no RDFS/OWL inference over the superclass axioms.
# health=2.5: DailyActivitySnapshot, DailySleepSnapshot and DailyVitalReading
#     dataclasses (the single-day history entries, distinct from the 7-day
#     ActivitySnapshot / SleepSnapshot aggregates), the five daily-snapshot
#     properties, and the four sleepQuality named individuals, which are read
#     and written as health: IRIs rather than string literals. Six wellness
#     container classes added with parse_wellness_container() / Pod.containers(),
#     which preserve rdf:List entry order. The five clinical record classes and
#     35 of the 40 v2.5 properties were already supported; those are covered by
#     tests here but were not newly implemented.
#     health:BloodPressureReading and health:HRVReading are NOT modelled, so
#     BloodPressureData and HRVData containers currently read with an empty
#     history.
# clinical=1.13: four vocabulary versions.
#     v1.10-v1.12 — clinical:hasEncounter, clinical:indicationReference,
#     clinical:parsedIndicationReference and clinical:linkedCondition added as
#     traversable IRI edges on the relevant models; the deprecated
#     clinical:linkedConditionIds literal is registered for READ ONLY so
#     existing data is not dropped, and is never written.
#     v1.13 — clinical:LabResult, clinical:Condition, clinical:Allergy and
#     clinical:Immunization are deprecated, not removed. The deserializer
#     accepts both spellings (DEPRECATED_TYPE_ALIASES); the serializer emits
#     only the health: forms. Also enforces the clinical v1.8
#     socialHistoryCategory value set, which VOCAB_VERSIONS claimed at v1.9 but
#     the validator did not check.
#     clinical:hasLabResult's v1.10 range correction needs no change here: this
#     SDK has no clinical:LaboratoryReport model, so the edge is unimplemented
#     rather than wrong.
#
# 2026-08-10 sync: core 3.5, health 2.6, clinical 1.14, coverage 1.4,
#     checkup 3.3. The previous pass deliberately left these rows behind
#     because the row would have been a claim the models could not back.
#
# core=3.5: cascade:sourceIdentity, the ORIGIN axis. Registered in
#     PROPERTY_PREDICATES (snake + camel) and carried on CascadeRecord, so
#     every record type has it: rdfs:domain is owl:Thing, and a property on a
#     subset of the models leaves the rest of the pod unreconcilable. The
#     value is a scheme-prefixed token (org: / ns: / transport:) and is
#     carried, not derived and NOT validated. The slug normalization is
#     defined in core.ttl and belongs to the producers that mint the value.
#     Deliberately kept distinct from cascade:sourceSystem (the INGESTION
#     batch, still unregistered here) and clinical:sourceEHR (a display
#     label). No other core v3.5 term needed model work.
# health=2.6: two changes.
#     health:interpretation is bound to the HL7 v3 ObservationInterpretation
#     code system (49 selectable codes, version 3.0.0) plus the
#     data-absent-reason code "unknown" plus the ten retained v2.5 words: 60
#     values, exported as OBSERVATION_INTERPRETATION_CODES /
#     OBSERVATION_INTERPRETATION_VALUES and as the ObservationInterpretation
#     type alias. LabInterpretation and VitalInterpretation now alias it; both
#     previously named "elevated", which no Cascade shape has ever accepted,
#     and omitted "high", which every one of them has. The list is pinned by
#     SHA-256 rather than by reading the shapes, because this repo's CI has no
#     spec checkout and a check that can skip is not a check.
#     health:labCategory, health:testCode, health:icd10Code and
#     health:snomedCode lost sh:maxCount 1. The four fields are list-typed on
#     LabResult and Condition; the serializer writes one repeated predicate
#     per value (NOT an rdf:List, which would be a single blank-node object
#     and fail the shapes' sh:datatype), and the deserializer groups repeated
#     predicates back into a sorted list.
# clinical=1.14: clinical:interpretation carries the same 60 values as
#     health:interpretation, so this SDK holds one set rather than two that
#     would have to be kept in step. clinical:snomedCode is multi-valued in
#     four shapes plus the new Encounter shape, so snomed_code is list-typed
#     on VitalSign, Procedure, Encounter and MedicationAdministration as well.
#     Encounter and MedicationAdministration remain serialize-only: neither is
#     registered in the deserializer, which predates this change.
#     The rest of v1.14 needs no code here. The widened clinical:cptCode
#     pattern, the date properties that now accept xsd:date, and the new
#     Encounter shape are all constraints this SDK never enforced, so there
#     was nothing rejecting them.
# coverage=1.4, checkup=3.3: no new terms this SDK models. Rowed so the drift
#     check reads what is true (that nothing here is behind) rather than
#     leaving a stale number that reads as unimplemented work.
#
# The value set IS enforced by validator.py, keyed on the property so it
#     covers health:interpretation and clinical:interpretation alike, with
#     exactly one documented exception: "elevated". That word is not in the
#     ratified set and the shapes reject it, but this SDK's own
#     LabInterpretation and VitalInterpretation named it through v1.5.0, and
#     conformance vital-001 / vital-004 are still POSITIVE fixtures carrying
#     it. See _SDK_LEGACY_INTERPRETATIONS for the removal trigger.
